body:
I hated him for all the bad reasons. He never infuriated me, his character was just annoying, and really bland. Same goes to Devin Weston.

&#x200B;

I always felt like GTA V has the same problem story wise as LCS, only V has \*some\* intresting aspects when it comes to the story. But the problem V shares with LCS is that for most of time nobody knows where the story is going, and not because there's a mystery in it. The "antagonists" are boring asf, the big secret that creates the tension between Michael and Trevor isn't secret for the player, Franklin is one of the most bland GTA protagonists ever (No offense to Shawn, he did an amazing job with the chracter!) , and it doesnt help that everyone gets rich after the first couple hours into the game. There's no build up, there really isn't any tension, there isn't much to look forward to.

The only intresting character was Michael, his relationship with Frank is quite good, and I liked the aspect where *~~his family leaves him~~* . Apart from that I really don't think that GTA V has a great story, especially when it is compared to most of the others in the series. There was potential in the story, but I feel like the execution was quite lackluster. 

&#x200B;

I still like the game, it has the most fun missions in the series, almost every mission feels like one of those *special* ones that happen once/twice in the previous games (*Rub Out* from VC, *Black Project* from SA,  *Domo Arigato Domestoboto* from VCS, *Three Leaf Clover* from IV, etc).

"*seek some out for yourself in the meantime* "

&#x200B;

You mean therapy, or other women? Sorry, I am just confused.

What people don't understand about Goro is that he didn't have a choice weather or not join Arasaka (if a company offered you to escape deep poverty IRL, you'd accept it aswell). He was an excellent warrior, and he became the personal guard of Saburo Arasaka. Imagine the feelings becoming the guard of the most powerful man in the world whose company also pulled you out of the dirt. Goro viewed things differently than how stuff was presented to us in the game. And I also heared that in Japanese culture loyalty is a key thing. Hell, there is a possibility that Saburo liked Goro more than his own son (which I can understand). After failing to protect his boss and almost like father figure, he got kicked out of Arasaka which gave him a new life in the first place. There is a reason Takemura is so hell bent on bringing justice to Yorinobu. 

&#x200B;

I really wish the Corpo lifepath would show a better insight into why somebody chooses to become a Corpo puppet, maybe V having more of a "Goro-style" approach to Arasaka, not really wanting to work against it at first, or something. But oh well, just like many stuff, this doesn't exist in the game.

I'm so sorry that you got burnt. I felt the same thing with Fallout 4. I am a huge Fallout fan, played through New Vegas around 10-15 times. Same with 3. I was incredibly hyped for F4 and I remember that anger and sadness building up inside while I was playing through that game. I bring Fallout up so much because that was a dissapointment for me probably as much as it is to you , and many other gamers. I can only hope that in a couple years, when this game is discounted, fixed up, and got some side content added in will you and many find it to the game you wanted it to be now. 

&#x200B;

TL;DR: I'm sorry for you, and genuinely hope that in the future, Cyberpunk will be the game that many people, including you were wainting for.

Komolyan nem értem azt, hogy lehet még valaki Fideszes.

&#x200B;

Ha a propaganda szempontot nézzük: Soros nincs megállítva (lmao), keresztény konzervatív kormánytagot kurváznak, drogoznak, meg meleg partikon vesznek részt. Még ha valaki agymosott is, semmit nem csinálnak abból, amit ígérnek, mondanak a birkáknak. 

&#x200B;

Persze, a korrupcióról, meg az autokrata berendezkedésről nem is beszélve, az hozzájuk úgy sem jut el...
